# Binaries
ogcode
*.exe

# Data directory
.ogcode/

# Workspace public folder — served over HTTP at /public for the web UI. Runtime
# and user artifacts land there; it is never part of the source tree. Anchored
# to the repo root so source asset folders (blog/public, web/public) stay
# trackable.
/public/

# Web build artifacts
# Dependencies
node_modules/
web/dist/
web/build/
web/.solid/

# Blog and docs build artifacts — the Pages workflow builds blog/ and
# docs-site/ into docs/blog and docs/docs before deploying, so the generated
# sites never live in the repo.
docs/blog/
blog/.astro/
docs/docs/
docs-site/.astro/

# Release build output (GoReleaser's default work dir — it archives the repo)
/dist/

# Python bytecode (bench harness)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Environment
.env

# Per-project ogcode config — local connection overrides (API keys, base URLs)
# that vary per machine. EnsureProjectFile extends an existing .gitignore with
# this pattern; it is also listed here so this repo never commits its own.
ogcode.json

# Winget manifests (managed by GoReleaser in winget-pkgs fork)
manifests/

# OS files
.DS_Store
*.swp

# Claude Code CLI
.claude/

# Stray skills install directory — an external skills installer wrote the
# golang-* skills here instead of .agents/skills, which is the directory
# ogcode actually discovers (internal/skill/discover.go). Root-anchored so no
# nested agent/ folder is swallowed.
/agent/

# Demo media — screen recordings and extracted frames kept machine-local;
# nothing in README/docs references them, so they must never land in the repo.
ogcode-demo.mp4
ogcode-live-demo.mov
ogcode-live-demo.mp4
demo-recording/

# Local scratch documents — planning notes kept machine-local, out of the
# published repo. Every rule is root-anchored (/), so it matches exactly one
# path and never a same-named file elsewhere: a bare `GIT_DIFF_PLAN.md` rule
# once silently swallowed the tracked `plans/GIT_DIFF_PLAN.md`.
/exponential_equations.tex
/polynomial_equations.pdf
/GIT_DIFF_PLAN.md
/MCP_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
/MCP_OAUTH_PLAN.md
/SKILL_FEATURE_IMPLEMENTATION.md

# Historical implementation plans whose features have shipped: the design
# record stays on the machine that wrote it. Code still cites two plans as the
# design of record — INCUS_WORKERS_PLAN.md (controlplane/) and
# MULTI_USER_REPOS_PLAN.md (Phase 4, not built) — and those two stay tracked.
/plans/ARCHITECTURE_AUDIT.md
/plans/BOARD_PUSH_PLAN.md
/plans/CONFLICT_FREE_MUTATIONS_PLAN.md
/plans/GIT_DIFF_PLAN.md
/plans/HOWTO_MD_PLAN.md
/plans/MCP_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
/plans/MCP_OAUTH_PLAN.md
/plans/MULTI_AGENT_COMMS_PLAN.md
/plans/REMOTE_AGENT_WORKERS_PLAN.md
/plans/RELEASE.md
/plans/SKILL_FEATURE_IMPLEMENTATION.md
/plans/TASK_SCHEDULING_PLAN.md
/plans/spreadsheet-index.md

# An empty AGENT.md placeholder: inert (LoadAgentMD skips a zero-byte file) and
# pointless in a fresh checkout, so it stays local.
/AGENT.md

# docs/DEPLOY.md is a redirect stub; the guide lives in the docs site
# (https://ogcode.in/docs/deployment/).
/docs/DEPLOY.md

# Project long-term memory — machine-local working notes, loaded at runtime by
# LoadMemoryMD from whatever directory ogcode is opened in. Never tracked: it is
# personal to a checkout, and it is re-sent in full on every model request, so a
# committed one becomes every contributor's per-turn token cost as well as ours.
MEMORY.md
# The two companions MEMORY.md delegates to — the dated log (HISTORY.md) and the
# verified procedures (HOWTO.md) — are equally local: neither is loaded into the
# prompt, both describe one checkout's own work, and a committed copy is dead
# weight for every other contributor. They stay on disk, never in git.
/HISTORY.md
/HOWTO.md
# Frozen pre-prune snapshots of the same file, kept beside it for reference.
/MEMORY-ARCHIVE.md

# Chrome Web Store upload builds (make extension-zip)
/ogweb-*.zip
